cpp/src/rt_manipulators_ik.cpp and cpp/include/rt_manipulators_ik.hpp reuse and
adapt samples/samples03 inverse-kinematics code from rt_manipulators_cpp.
cpp/src/x7_controller.cpp combines that solver with project-specific wrist
orientation decomposition, branch selection, continuity handling and command
submission. cpp/config/ contains CRANE-X7 model/configuration material derived
from the RT sample configuration.

The downloaded rt_manipulators_lib is modified by
third_party/patches/recording-feedback.patch: hardware.hpp, hardware.cpp and the
new recording_feedback.hpp provide timestamped position feedback for recording.
These files are modified versions, not an unmodified upstream distribution.

OpenTeleVision
Copyright [2024] [Xuxin Cheng, Jialong Li, Shiqi Yang, Ge Yang and Xiaolong Wang]

The Python teleoperation layer is adapted from OpenTeleVision/TeleVision,
particularly TeleVision.py and the preprocessing/streaming workflow. Project
changes include CRANE-X7 relative wrist control, Vuer payload decoding, UVC
capture/rectification, bounded video transport, recording and action replay.
It is not an unmodified distribution of OpenTeleVision.

